# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-go-rubygems-composer  (artifact-keeper
# 1.12.0: #4103 Go, #4104 RubyGems, #4105 Composer, epic #4097)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (a Go module proxy,
# a RubyGems source and a Composer repository whose packages carry known
# identities). LOCAL-ONLY: the verdicts come from the backend image's bundled
# Grype and its pre-seeded vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no
# internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: before 1.12.0 a Go, RubyGems or Composer Remote (or a
# Virtual over one) with scan_on_proxy=true streamed every proxied package
# unscanned (200, no X-AK-Scan) and /api/v1/formats reported the three as
# `accepted`. 1.12.0 routes module zips, .gem files and dist archives through
# the shared inline scan gate: vulnerable -> 403 scan_blocked, clean -> 200
# X-AK-Scan: clean with the verdict reused, a package whose own metadata does
# not back the requested coordinate -> 423 under fail_closed with no verdict
# row, fail_open -> served pending then blocked once the async verdict lands,
# record_only -> served X-AK-Scan: recorded; metadata stays unscanned.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: an image carrying artifact-keeper#4103-#4105.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
